  "summary": "Like Short Spine but the legs stay straight: roll up onto the upper back with long legs, then roll down bone by bone.",
  "steps": [
    "Headrest down. Feet in the long loops, legs straight up just in front of the hips.",
    "Breathe out, tip the pelvis and peel the spine up until the weight rests across the upper back.",
    "Breathe in to pause.",
    "Breathe out to roll down one bone at a time, legs still long.",
    "Finish by pressing the long legs down towards the springs and back up."
  ],
  "layers": [
    {
      "tag": "L1",
      "title": "Roll up and down",
      "text": "Legs together all the way."
    },
